Signature:  (a : ℚ) : a.floor = a.num / a.den

5. [THEOREM] Floor of Rational Number as Integer Division of Numerator by Denominator
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Floor
Name: Rat.floor_def
Description: For any rational number $q = \frac{m}{n}$ where $m$ is the numerator and $n$ is the denominator, the floor of $q$ is equal to the integer division of $m$ by $n$, i.e., $\lfloor q \rfloor = m / n$.
Signature:  {q : ℚ} : ⌊q⌋ = q.num / q.den

6. [THEOREM] Difference Between Element and Its Fractional Part Equals Floor
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Floor
Name: Int.self_sub_fract
Description: For any element $a$ in a linearly ordered ring $\alpha$, the difference between $a$ and its fractional part $\operatorname{fract}(a)$ equals the floor of $a$, i.e., $a - \operatorname{fract}(a) = \lfloor a \rfloor$.
Signature:  (a : α) : a - fract a = ⌊a⌋

