8. [THEOREM] Difference Equals Fractional Part: $a - \lfloor a \rfloor = \operatorname{fract}(a)$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Floor
Name: Int.self_sub_floor
Description: For any element $a$ in a linearly ordered ring $\alpha$, the difference between $a$ and its floor $\lfloor a \rfloor$ equals the fractional part of $a$, i.e., $a - \lfloor a \rfloor = \operatorname{fract}(a)$.
