4. [THEOREM] Floor Equals Zero if and only if Element is in $[0, 1)$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Floor
Name: Int.floor_eq_zero_iff
Description: For any element $a$ in a linearly ordered ring $\alpha$ with a floor function, the floor of $a$ equals $0$ if and only if $a$ belongs to the interval $[0, 1)$. In other words, $\lfloor a \rfloor = 0 \leftrightarrow a \in [0, 1)$.
