5. [THEOREM] Characterization of Floor Function: $\lfloor a \rfloor = z \leftrightarrow z \leq a < z + 1$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Floor
Name: Int.floor_eq_iff
Description: For any element $a$ in a linearly ordered ring $\alpha$ with a floor function and any integer $z$, the floor of $a$ equals $z$ if and only if the following two conditions hold:
1. The coercion of $z$ into $\alpha$ satisfies $(z : \alpha) \leq a$.
2. $a$ is strictly less than $z + 1$.

In other words, $\lfloor a \rfloor = z \leftrightarrow z \leq a < z + 1$.
Signature:  : ⌊a⌋ = z ↔ ↑z ≤ a ∧ a < z + 1

