From (4) and (11),

\[
0\le n\frac{s-r}{s+r}<1
\;\Longleftrightarrow\;
0\le n<\frac{s+r}{s-r}. \tag{13}
\]

Hence the possible values of `n` are exactly  

\[
n=1,2,\dots ,N,
\qquad\text{where}\qquad
N:=\Bigl\lfloor\frac{s+r}{s-r}\Bigr\rfloor . \tag{14}
\]

Because `s` and `r` are coprime, the fraction \((s+r)/(s-r)\) is
