\((s-r)^{2}\)) transforms (18) into the integer equation

\[
r\,s = 210\,(s-r)^{2}. \tag{19}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6.  Solving the Diophantine equation

Put \(d:=s-r>0\).  Then \(s=r+d\) and (19) becomes

\[
r(r+d)=210\,d^{2}
\;\Longleftrightarrow\;
r^{2}+rd-210d^{2}=0. \tag{20}
\]

