\[
a=\frac{s^{2}-r^{2}}{4s^{2}}
  =\frac{(15d)^{2}-(14d)^{2}}{4\,(15d)^{2}}
  =\frac{225d^{2}-196d^{2}}{900d^{2}}
  =\frac{29}{900}. \tag{22}
\]

The fraction \(\frac{29}{900}\) is already in lowest terms
(\(\gcd(29,900)=1\)), hence

\[
a.\text{num}=29,\qquad a.\text{den}=900. \tag{23}
\]

Finally

\[
a.\text{den}+a.\text{num}=900+29=929,
\]

which is exactly the desired conclusion (3). ∎

