   This contradicts `h₀ : Nat.Prime p ∧ Nat.Prime q`.

9. **Conclude.**  
   The assumption that `p·q-(p+q)=194` leads to a contradiction with the given primality of `p` and `q`. Therefore the equality cannot hold; i.e.

   \[
   \uparrow p * \uparrow q - (\uparrow p + \uparrow q) \neq (194 : \mathbb N).
   \]

∎

