   Cancelling \(\pi\) from (6) and multiplying by \(180\) gives  

   \[
   m = 35\cdot\frac{180}{72}
     = 35\cdot\frac{5}{2}
     = \frac{175}{2}.
   \tag{7}
   \]

   Thus \(m\) is the rational number \(\displaystyle\frac{175}{2}\).

9. **Identify numerator and denominator of \(m\).**  
   The rational \(\frac{175}{2}\) is already in lowest terms because
   \(\gcd(175,2)=1\).  Hence  

   \[
   m.\text{num}=175,\qquad m.\text{den}=2 .
