   \[
   S:=\sum_{k=1}^{35}\sin(k\theta).
   \]

2. **Recall a standard trigonometric sum identity.**  
   For any real \(\alpha\) and any integer \(n\ge 2\),

   \[
   \sum_{k=1}^{n-1}\sin(k\alpha)
   =\frac{\sin\!\bigl(\frac{n\alpha}{2}\bigr)\,
          \sin\!\bigl(\frac{(n-1)\alpha}{2}\bigr)}
         {\sin\!\bigl(\frac{\alpha}{2}\bigr)} .
   \tag{1}
   \]

   *Proof of (1).*  
   Using the addition formula  

   \[
   \sin x+\sin y = 2\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{x+y}{2}\Bigr)
                     \cos\!\Bigl(\frac{x-y}{2}\Bigr)
