2. [THEOREM] Point Below Segment Characterization via Slope Comparison: $f(c) \leq \text{lineMap}(f(a), f(b))(r) \leftrightarrow \text{slope}(f, a, c) \leq \text{slope}(f, c, b)$
Module: Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.AffineSpace.Ordered
Name: map_le_lineMap_iff_slope_le_slope
Description: Let $f \colon k \to PE$ be a function from a field $k$ to an affine space $PE$ over $k$, and let $a, b \in k$ with $a < b$. For $r \in k$ with $0 < r < 1$, define $c = (1-r)a + rb$. Then the point $(c, f(c))$ lies on or below the line segment connecting $(a, f(a))$ and $(b, f(b))$ if and only if the slope of $f$ between $a$ and $c$ is less than or equal to the slope of $f$ between $c$ and $b$.

In other words:
\[ f(c) \leq (1-r)f(a) + r f(b) \leftrightarrow \frac{f(c)-f(a)}{c-a} \leq \frac{f(b)-f(c)}{b-c} \]
Signature:  (hab : a < b) (h₀ : 0 < r) (h₁ : r < 1) : f c ≤ lineMap (f a) (f b) r ↔ slope f a c ≤ slope f c b

