3. [DEFINITION] Linear combination tactic for commutative rings
Module: Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination
Name: Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination.elabLinearCombination
Description: The tactic `linear_combination` simplifies a goal in a commutative ring by forming a linear combination of given equalities or inequalities and subtracting it from the target. The tactic can also accept a normalization tactic to further simplify the resulting expression. For ordered algebraic structures (like linearly ordered commutative rings), it supports taking linear combinations of inequalities as well.

The tactic works by:
1. Creating a weighted sum of the provided equations/inequalities with given coefficients.
2. Subtracting the right-hand side of this weighted sum from both sides of the target, setting the right-hand side to zero.
3. Setting the new goal to be the equality/inequality between the left-hand sides of the modified target and weighted sum.
4. Applying a normalization tactic to the resulting expression.
Signature:  (tk : Syntax) (norm? : Option Syntax.Tactic) (exp? : Option Syntax.NumLit) (input : Option Syntax.Term) :
  Tactic.TacticM Unit

