Name: Function.Periodic.mul_const'
Description: Let $\alpha$ be a division semiring and $f : \alpha \to \beta$ be a periodic function with period $c \in \alpha$. Then for any $a \in \alpha$, the function $x \mapsto f(x \cdot a)$ is periodic with period $c / a$.
Signature:  [DivisionSemiring α] (h : Periodic f c) (a : α) : Periodic (fun x => f (x * a)) (c / a)

3. [THEOREM] Periodic Function Invariance Under Translation by Integer Multiples of the Period
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Periodic
Name: Function.Periodic.map_vadd_zmultiples
Description: Let $\alpha$ be an additive commutative group and let $f : \alpha \to \beta$ be a periodic function with period $c \in \alpha$. For any element $a$ in the additive subgroup generated by $c$ (i.e., $a \in \mathbb{Z}\cdot c$) and any $x \in \alpha$, we have $f(a + x) = f(x)$.
Signature:  [AddCommGroup α] (hf : Periodic f c) (a : AddSubgroup.zmultiples c) (x : α) : f (a +ᵥ x) = f x

4. [THEOREM] Evaluation of Polynomial Multiplied by Constant: $\text{eval}_2(f, x)(p \cdot C(a)) = \text{eval}_2(f, x)(p) \cdot f(a)$ under Commutativity
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs
Name: Polynomial.eval₂_mul_C'
Description: Let $R$ and $S$ be semirings, $f \colon R \to S$ a ring homomorphism, and $x \in S$ an element. For any polynomial $p \in R[X]$ and element $a \in R$, if $f(a)$ commutes with $x$ (i.e., $f(a) \cdot x = x \cdot f(a)$), then the evaluation of $p \cdot C(a)$ at $x$ via $f$ equals the product of the evaluation of $p$ at $x$ via $f$ and $f(a)$:
$$ \text{eval}_2(f, x)(p \cdot C(a)) = \text{eval}_2(f, x)(p) \cdot f(a). $$
Signature:  (h : Commute (f a) x) : eval₂ f x (p * C a) = eval₂ f x p * f a

5. [THEOREM] Periodic Function Invariance under Translation by Multiples of Period
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Periodic
Name: Function.Periodic.map_vadd_multiples
Description: Let $f : \alpha \to \beta$ be a periodic function with period $c$ in an additive commutative monoid $\alpha$. Then for any element $a$ in the additive submonoid generated by $c$ (i.e., $a \in \text{AddSubmonoid.multiples}(c)$) and any $x \in \alpha$, we have $f(a + x) = f(x)$.
Signature:  [AddCommMonoid α] (hf : Periodic f c) (a : AddSubmonoid.multiples c) (x : α) : f (a +ᵥ x) = f x
