Thus the theorem is not provable from the given premise; the statement is mathematically incorrect.

To make the theorem true one needs an additional assumption that forces the stronger relation \((\*)\). For example, assuming that \(f\) is linear (or that \(f\) is injective, or that \(f\) satisfies \(f(f a)=2f a+f(0)\) explicitly) would allow the conclusion to be derived.
