\(g(2x)=2g(x)\).  This condition constrains the values of \(f\) on even integers, but it imposes **no restriction** on the values of \(f\) on odd integers.  Consequently many functions satisfy the hypothesis without being additive (up to a constant).

For a concrete counter‑example, define  

* \(f(0)=0\),  
