Module: Mathlib.Data.ENat.Basic
Name: ENat.map_add
Description: Let $\beta$ be a type with an addition operation, and let $F$ be a type of functions from $\mathbb{N}$ to $\beta$ that preserves addition. For any function $f \in F$ and extended natural numbers $a, b \in \mathbb{N}^\infty$, the map of the sum $a + b$ under $f$ equals the sum of the maps of $a$ and $b$ under $f$, i.e., $(a + b).map\ f = a.map\ f + b.map\ f$.
