2. [DEFINITION] Construction of linear map from linearity conditions
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs
Name: IsLinearMap.mk'
Description: Given a map $f \colon M \to M₂$ between modules over a semiring $R$ that satisfies the linearity conditions (additivity and homogeneity), this constructs a bundled linear map of type $M \toₗ[R] M₂$.

The linearity conditions are:
1. $f(x + y) = f(x) + f(y)$ for all $x, y \in M$
2. $f(c \cdot x) = c \cdot f(x)$ for all $c \in R$ and $x \in M$
Signature:  (f : M → M₂) (lin : IsLinearMap R f) : M →ₗ[R] M₂

3. [THEOREM] Reflection Map is Involutive
Module: Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Reflection
Name: Module.involutive_reflection
Description: Let $M$ be a module over a commutative ring $R$, let $x \in M$, and let $f \in M^*$ be a linear form such that $f(x) = 2$. Then the reflection map $y \mapsto y - (f y) \cdot x$ is an involution, i.e., applying it twice returns the original input: $\text{reflection}_x(f) \circ \text{reflection}_x(f) = \text{id}_M$.
Signature:  (h : f x = 2) : Involutive (reflection h)

